      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) such that \\( h(x) = x \\), we need to determine the function \\( h(x) \\) first. We are given the equation \\( h(4x-1) = 2x + 7 \\).\n\nLet's denote \\( y = 4x - 1 \\). We need to express \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\). Solving for \\( x \\), we get:\n\\[ y = 4x - 1 \\]\n\\[ y + 1 = 4x \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{y + 1}{4} \\]\n\nNow substitute \\( x = \\frac{y + 1}{4} \\) into the given equation \\( h(4x-1) = 2x + 7 \\):\n\\[ h(y) = 2 \\left( \\frac{y + 1}{4} \\right) + 7 \\]\n\\[ h(y) = \\frac{2(y + 1)}{4} + 7 \\]\n\\[ h(y) = \\frac{2y + 2}{4} + 7 \\]\n\\[ h(y) = \\frac{y + 1}{2} + 7 \\]\n\\[ h(y) = \\frac{y + 1 + 14}{2} \\]\n\\[ h(y) = \\frac{y + 15}{2} \\]\n\nSo, the function \\( h(x) \\) is:\n\\[ h(x) = \\frac{x + 15}{2} \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( x \\) such that \\( h(x) = x \\):\n\\[ \\frac{x + 15}{2} = x \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), multiply both sides by 2:\n\\[ x + 15 = 2x \\]\n\\[ 15 = 2x - x \\]\n\\[ 15 = x \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{15} \\]",
